course: dictionary
lesson: 5879
title: Mangrove: a tree with its feet in the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mangrove is a tree that grows in salty water along warm coasts, with tangled roots standing up above the mud. The words around a new word give you clues. «Most trees die if you pour salty sea water on their roots, but mangroves grow with their feet in it.» The word but tells you mangroves are different from most trees: they can live in salt water.
explain: A mangrove can also name a place. A mangrove swamp or mangrove forest is an area of coast covered with these trees. «Their tangled roots break the waves and hold the soil» shows why scientists and geographers care about them. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A «mangrove» is a tree or shrub that grows in salty water along tropical coasts.
fact: A «mangrove swamp» or «mangrove forest» is an area of coast covered with mangroves.
fact: Mangroves are a nursery for young fish, crabs and birds, and their roots shelter them.
fact: Mangroves are being cut down for shrimp farms and building, so people work to protect and replant them.
exercise: «Mangroves grow with their feet in salty water along warm coasts.» Where do mangroves grow? | On mountain tops, far from the sea | *Along warm tropical coasts, in salty water | In deserts, where there is no water | In the middle of cold lakes
exercise: «Their tangled roots break the waves and hold the soil, like a sponge and a fence in one.» What jobs do mangrove roots do? | They grow flowers for the bees | *They break the waves and hold the soil | They make the sea taste sweet | They float away to other islands
exercise: «Mangrove seeds sprout while still on the tree, drop as long spikes, and can float for months.» Find and copy one word that means start to grow. | months | *sprout | float | spikes
test: «Tigers swim between islands in the Sundarbans mangroves of India and Bangladesh.» Where are the Sundarbans mangroves? | In Florida | In northern Australia | In the Sahara desert | *In India and Bangladesh
test: Which phrase names an area of coast covered with these trees? | mangrove seed | salt crystals | mangrove roots | *mangrove swamp
exam: Why are mangroves important? | They grow only in deserts | They make the sea colder | *They shelter baby fish, crabs and birds, and protect coasts from storms | They are only useful for making shrimp farms
